rl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-4x3.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-4x3.webp","width":1200,"height":900,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","description":"The wide beach in downtown Myrtle Beach at low tide, with the SkyWheel, rows of blue umbrellas and towers along the shore","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Tom Long"},"creditText":"Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myrtle_Beach_(24050832475).jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myrtle_Beach_(24050832475).jpg"},{"@type":"ImageObject","contentUrl":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-16x9.webp","url":"https://chapter3realty.com/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-16x9.webp","width":1200,"height":675,"encodingFormat":"image/webp","description":"The wide beach in downtown Myrtle Beach at low tide, with the SkyWheel, rows of blue umbrellas and towers along the shore","creator":{"@type":"Person","name":"Tom Long"},"creditText":"Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0, via Wikimedia Commons","copyrightNotice":"© Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0","license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/","acquireLicensePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myrtle_Beach_(24050832475).jpg","isBasedOn":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Myrtle_Beach_(24050832475).jpg"}],"mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://chapter3realty.com/buyers/buying-in-myrtle-beach/"},"about":{"@type":"Thing","name":"Buying a home in Myrtle Beach and Horry County, South Carolina"},"keywords":"Myrtle Beach buyer's market, buying in Myrtle Beach, is Myrtle Beach a buyers market, Myrtle Beach housing market, how much is a house in Myrtle Beach, steps to buying a house in South Carolina, South Carolina attorney closing, buying a house in South Carolina from out of state, CL-100"}</script>
+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Myrtle Beach a buyer's market?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For condos, yes: about 7.5 months of supply, past the 5 to 7 months of a balanced local market. For houses, not yet: about 4 months. Houses at $700,000 and up are near the point where buyers gain the edge."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Will home prices in Myrtle Beach go down?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not forecast prices. The federal house price index for Horry County was about flat in the year to mid-2026, after rising about 51 percent from mid-2021 to mid-2025. More than half of the homes for sale have cut their asking price."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a lawyer to buy a house in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every South Carolina home closing must be supervised by a South Carolina attorney. With a home loan for personal or family use, the lender must ask which attorney you want and follow your choice."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take to close on a house in South Carolina?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As long as the closing date you and the seller write into the contract. With a loan, federal rules add two waits: the Loan Estimate within three business days of applying, and the Closing Disclosure at least three business days before closing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a CL-100?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The termite letter, the Official South Carolina Wood Infestation Report. Only a licensed pest control applicator may issue it for a sale or a loan. It reports visible insect damage, active infestations, and moisture and decay under the house."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What time of year do the fewest homes sell in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"January and February. Recorded resales were fewest then, about 430 houses a month, and were about 620 to 670 a month from May to October."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I rent my Myrtle Beach condo by the night?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Inside the City of Myrtle Beach, about 3 in 4 condos are in zones that allow rentals under 90 days. In North Myrtle Beach a short-term rental needs a business license. A condo's own rules can still ban them."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between a condo and a condotel?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A condotel is a condo in a building run like a hotel: a front desk, daily cleaning or a rule that owners join the rental program, for example. Fannie Mae will not back a loan there."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are property taxes in Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On a house the county values at $350,000, the 2026 tax inside the City of Myrtle Beach is about $1,410 a year if you live in it. As a second home it is about $5,350. Outside the cities it is about $1,290 and $4,220."}}]}</script>
