}main#main .bm .cap{display:block;font-family:var(--sans);font-weight:700;color:var(--navy);font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.35;margin:0 0 .7rem}main#main .bm-key{list-style:none;margin:0 0 .9rem;padding:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.35rem 1rem;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.35;color:var(--navy)}main#main .bm-key li{margin:0;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.4rem}main#main .bm-key i{flex:0 0 auto;width:.95rem;height:.95rem;border-radius:4px}main#main .bm h3.bm-g{font-family:var(--sans)!important;font-size:.82rem!important;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8a5226!important;font-weight:700;margin:.6rem 0 .35rem!important}main#main .bm ol{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:.55rem}main#main .bm-r{margin:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,15rem) minmax(0,1fr);align-items:center;gap:.2rem .9rem;font-family:var(--sans);color:var(--navy)}main#main .bm-n{font-size:1rem;line-height:1.3}main#main .bm-all .bm-n{font-weight:700}main#main .bm-t{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 5.7rem;align-items:center;gap:.5rem}main#main .bm-k{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:1.6rem;border-radius:6px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent 50%,rgba(28,32,40,.08) 50%,rgba(28,32,40,.08) 70%,transparent 70%)}main#main .bm-b{display:block;height:1.05rem;border-radius:999px;min-width:.6rem}main#main .bm-all .bm-b{height:1.35rem}main#main .bm-b.sell,main#main .bm-key i.sell{background:#3d6f93}main#main .bm-b.bal,main#main .bm-key i.bal{background:#b59a77}main#main .bm-b.buy,main#main .bm-key i.buy{background:#c4783a}main#main .bm-key i.band{background:rgba(28,32,40,.12)}main#main .bm-v{white-space:nowrap;font-size:1rem;font-weight:700}main#main .bm-v small{font-size:.9rem;font-weight:500;color:var(--muted)}main#main .bm figcaption{margin-top:.85rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.55}@media (max-width:599px){main#main .bm{padding:1rem .85rem .9rem}main#main .bm-r{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:.15rem}main#main .bm ol{gap:.7rem}}</style><figure class="bm" role="group" aria-label="Months of homes for sale at the past year's pace of sales, Horry County, condos and houses by price"><span class="cap">How many months it would take to sell every home for sale</span><ul class="bm-key" role="list"><li><i class="sell"></i>Sellers have the edge (under 5)</li><li><i class="bal"></i>Balanced (5 to 7)</li><li><i class="buy"></i>Buyers have room (over 7)</li><li><i class="band"></i>Shaded: 5 to 7 months</li></ul><h3 class="bm-g">Condos</h3><ol><li class="bm-r bm-all"><span class="bm-n">All condos</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b buy" style="width:75.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">7.5<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Condos under $150K</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b bal" style="width:67.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">6.7<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Condos $150K to $250K</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b buy" style="width:85.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">8.5<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Condos $250K to $400K</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b bal" style="width:67.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">6.7<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Condos $400K and up</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b buy" style="width:79.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">7.9<small> months</small></b></span></li></ol><h3 class="bm-g">Houses</h3><ol><li class="bm-r bm-all"><span class="bm-n">All houses</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b sell" style="width:38.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">3.8<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Houses under $300K</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b sell" style="width:33.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">3.3<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Houses $300K to $450K</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b sell" style="width:32.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">3.2<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Houses $450K to $700K</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b sell" style="width:44.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">4.4<small> months</small></b></span></li><li class="bm-r"><span class="bm-n">Houses $700K and up</span><span class="bm-t"><span class="bm-k"><i class="bm-b bal" style="width:72.0%"></i></span><b class="bm-v">7.2<small> months</small></b></span></li></ol><figcaption>Homes for sale today against homes sold in the past year, builders' sales included. Houses include townhouses and manufactured homes. The bar's scale runs to 10 months.</figcaption></figure><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">On a condo, there is room to ask for a lower price or for repairs. On a house under $700,000 there is less room: the houses for sale would sell out in about half the time the condos would.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Sellers already feel it. More than half of the homes for sale have cut their asking price. About 4 in 10 houses and more than half of condos for sale have been listed more than 90 days.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">House prices have stopped climbing. The federal house price index for Horry County rose about 51 percent from mid-2021 to mid-2025. In the year to mid-2026 it was about flat. The index tracks houses, not condos.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Sales follow the season. Recorded resales were fewest in January and February, about 430 houses a month, and were about 620 to 670 a month from May to October.</p><div class="c3-aerial"><figure class="c3ph-hero" style=""><div class="c3ph-f"><img src="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-1200w.webp" srcset="/images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-600w.webp 600w, /images/2026-11-a/buyers-buying-in-myrtle-beach/myrtle-beach-skywheel-beach-1200w.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1136px" width="1200" height="675" alt="The wide beach in downtown Myrtle Beach at low tide, with the SkyWheel, rows of blue umbrellas and towers along the shore" loading="lazy" decoding="async"><span class="c3ph-cr"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Photo: Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0. License: CC BY-SA 2.0" title="License: CC BY-SA 2.0">Photo: Tom Long, CC BY-SA 2.0</a></span></div><figcaption>The beach beside the SkyWheel in downtown Myrtle Beach. In the city, about 3 in 4 homes for sale are condos.</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--ivory)" id="by-town"><div class="wrap"><h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;line-height:1.3" data-toc="Town by town">Where in Myrtle Beach do buyers have the most room to negotiate?</h2><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">In the City of Myrtle Beach, condos have about a year of supply, the most of any town here. Houses in Surfside Beach, Little River, Carolina Forest, Forestbrook and Red Hill have under 4 months.</p><p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:720px;margin-bottom:1rem">Many buyers say "Myrtle Beach" for the whole coast. The map and the table split it into ten towns and communities, from Little River to Garden City and inland to Conway.</p><div class="c3b-map"><figure style="margin:1.8rem 0;max-width:760px"><svg style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" id="c3r-ten-town